  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-domain:real-l2-positive-square-commutation",
    "anchor": "PBPS2609.06905v1 Appendix D.1 spectral calculus background;ASTIS positive real-L2 square commutation corollary for B23/B21.",
    "original_text": "Fan Chen,Sinho Chewi,Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang supply Appendix D.1 spectral-calculus background. This ASTIS auxiliary real-L2 corollary uses pinned Mathlib CFC and local complexification;it is not a separately printed theorem.\nFor every measurable space Ω and every measure μ,let G,D be bounded real linear operators on real L²(μ). Assume G,D positive:selfadjoint with nonnegative quadratic form. If G²D=DG²,then GD=DG. No probability,finite measure,finite-dimensional L²,nontriviality or caller CFC instance is required. This ASTIS auxiliary consequence of unique positive-root functional calculus is not a separately printed PBPS theorem. Its actual paper consumer internally proves D=I+T positive and G² commuting with D;these are not extra paper premises.\nPBPS2609.06905v1 Appendix D.1 spectral calculus background;ASTIS positive real-L2 square commutation corollary for B23/B21.",
    "text_sha256": "509e73b850c3c7a4f0600ba00a4fa80bc1b2b8ab76cf31bb8d9520d1a3219e9b"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareCommute.positive_square_commutation",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Measure/L2RealSquareCommute.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)\n    (G D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ)\n    (hG : G.IsPositive) (hD : D.IsPositive)\n    (hCommute : Commute (G*G) D) : Commute G D",
    "statement_sha256": "c58d138c8c2d371b326aefbec51d51f2405985901a2370714726484487f3a892",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let Omega be an arbitrary measurable space, let mu be any measure on Omega, and let H=Lp(R,2,mu), the real Hilbert space of square-integrable measurable functions modulo mu-almost-everywhere equality. Let G,D:H->H be bounded real-linear operators. Assume G and D are positive: symmetric/selfadjoint with nonnegative real quadratic form. Assume the square G composed with G commutes with D, that is\n  (G composed with G) composed with D = D composed with (G composed with G).\nThen G commutes with D:\n  G composed with D = D composed with G.\nAll Omega, its measurable structure, mu,G,D are universally quantified. Both positivity hypotheses are retained even if one might be unnecessary in another theorem. Multiplication means composition of bounded endomorphisms of this same real Hilbert space. There is no finite-mass, probability, finite-dimensionality, invertibility, gap, nontriviality, or caller functional-calculus hypothesis. Zero-space and admissible zero-operator cases are included. No output witnesses, derived measures, kernel, or link to another packet is part of this proposition.",
    "text_sha256": "7a286220178225f9bc7b2eb3cc19207a095bc7bea47178c84239d0426ee9ea9d",
    "decoder": "/root/anonymous_decoder64",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "6a04e37df8b274088621d1ffdead01702bd51e50bd532cb2c8706a82ea3d497f",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "22bd980f4390e913eb6ac12ba2fb98f5cb5c25d2de6e5f10e3d45dac6a2e3589",
    "source_text_visible": false
